# Pilldue — project context

Personal local medication refill tracker. .NET 10, Spectre.Console, WPF host, EF Core + SQLite.

## Product

- Refill day is each medication's prescription start day-of-month.
- Med: package size, prescribed package count, pills per dose, dose interval, stock, prescription length (~6 months).
- Flows: stock vs next/second refill, refill by packages (today), skip-dose, missed dose, calendar.
- Out of scope: pharmacy/doctor contacts, dose reminders, multi-user/cloud.
- Details: `docs/use-cases.md`, `docs/architecture.md`.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/Pilldue.Business` | Domain, ports, planning, in-memory fakes, UI catalogs. No EF. |
| `src/Pilldue.Data` | EF Core + SQLite, migrations, config file, `PilldueComposition` |
| `src/Pilldue.UI` | Spectre screens. Business only. |
| `src/Pilldue.UI.Wpf` | WPF screens. Business only. |
| `src/Pilldue.App` | Terminal host |
| `src/Pilldue.UI.Desktop` | WPF host (Windows). Composition root for the desktop screens. |
| `tests/` | Business, Data, UI, Integration |
| `docs/` | Human docs |

**Direction:** App → UI + Data. Desktop → Data + UI.Wpf + Business. UI → Business. UI.Wpf → Business. Data → Business. Screen projects must not reference Data. UI catalogs live in Business (`UiLocalizer`).

## Non-negotiables

- Branches: `<issue>-<slug>` (`8-refill-dates`). No `feature/` prefix. PRs target `main`. Do not push commits to `main`.
- Track work on GitHub Issues and one Project (`issue-tracking`). One issue per branch and PR.
- Schema changes go through EF migrations in `Pilldue.Data`. No Dapper or hand-rolled ADO.
- New UI copy: the same key in both `UiLocalizer` catalogs (English and Serbian Latin).
- Update `docs/` when a decision changes.
- Do not change port signatures without a contracts follow-up.

## Parallel agents

One issue per worktree (`ticket-worktree`). Use a cheaper model for helpers, thin UI, and isolated CRUD. Use a stronger model for EF migrations, cross-layer wiring, and hard rebases. If a cheaper agent fails twice on the same issue, retry with a stronger model.

## Task → rule

| Task | Rule |
|------|------|
| Track issues and the project board | `issue-tracking`, skill `github-ticket-flow` |
| Start implementation | `ticket-worktree` |
| Where code goes | `layer-structure`, `model-separation` |
| SQLite schema | `migrations` |
| UI strings | `localization-both-resx` |
| Tests | `testing` |
| Open PR | `create-pr` (explicit `@create-pr` + issue id, from that worktree) |
| Review a PR | `review-pr` (explicit `@review-pr` + PR number) |
| Refactor / new pattern | `refactoring-and-rules` |

Index: `implementation-rules-index`.
